# Template sync record
#
# Why this repository differs from `template/main` where it does. Read by a
# person; no tool parses it.
#
# THE CHECK IS A DERIVATION, NOT THIS FILE:
#
#   for f in docs/convention/*.md; do
#     git diff --numstat HEAD template/main -- "$f"
#   done
#
# Every file that comes back differing is either named in `skipped` below with
# the decision that owns it, or has not been considered. That is the whole
# protocol, and it reads what is true now rather than what was true when
# somebody last wrote a line here.
#
# A DIFFERING FILE IS NOT AUTOMATICALLY A STALE ONE. Before treating any
# difference as an update to take, ask whether the file was ever a template
# copy at all:
#
#   git hash-object docs/convention/<file>
#   for c in $(git rev-list template/main -- docs/convention/<file>); do
#     git rev-parse "$c:docs/convention/<file>"
#   done
#
# A matching blob anywhere in that list means the file IS an older template
# copy and the difference is staleness. NO match means it is a local
# adaptation, and a checkout from the template would overwrite decisions
# nobody has enumerated while reporting success. The diff cannot tell those
# apart: both look like lines that differ.
#
# `last-audited` below is a bookmark and nothing verifies it. It is a
# convenience for narrowing `git log`, not the check: if it goes stale the
# derivation still gives the right answer, and a reader who trusts it instead
# of running the derivation gets the older one.

